= Constitutional Court rules on the Climate Change Law

Even with the Constitutional Court preserving the very broad framework of the Climate Change Law, including adaptation and Catalan transition measures, it has nontheless annulled many of the stated targets and obligations. We can assume some of the goals of maturing into a green economy will surive and still have a purpose, but without many of the compulsory economy-wide provisions we're yet to see how effective it will be. 

